  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nRidging will dominate the pattern today, bringing well above\nnormal temperatures to the area. Expect highs in the 70s today \nalong with dry conditions. A favorable pressure gradient over the \nParadise Valley will result in increased winds along the Beartooth\nFoothills into this evening, with gusts in the 30s to 50 mph. The\nlatest probability for gusts of at least 50 mph for around \nLivingston and Nye is 50 to 70 percent. The probability for gusts \nof 60 mph or greater is around 20 to 30 percent.\n\nA dry cold front is shown by models moving through the region\ntonight, this will bring cooler temperatures for Sunday with highs\nin the 50s and 60s. Ensembles show ridging rebuilding Monday and \nTuesday, bringing temperatures back into the 60s and low 70s.\n\nUncertainty remains high for the middle of next week, though\nguidance is showing a low digging along the West Coast. The latest\nforecast has a low chance of precipitation coming into the\nmountains southwest of Billings late Tuesday into Wednesday at\nthis time. Continue to monitor the forecast as the weekend\nprogresses.\n\nMatos",
